  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="20c6f97f-8328-57bd-9fb8-d8eedf6146cf" activityNameId="3468f839-9401-5a39-ae04-b0e868beec6f" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Biogas, from agricultural co-digestion, not covered, at storage</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Biogas, from agricultural co-digestion, not covered, at storage
The data represent a mixed manure (50% cattle and 50% swines) digested with a cosubstrate. The co-substrate accounts for  20% of the total input.  As a first approximation we assume that the co-substrate is identical with average biowaste.  Liquid manure input is assumed to have a share of dry matter of 7.5%,  and an organic share of dry matter of 80% with a carbon content of 50%.  All emissions are exclusively allocated to the installation and operation of the agricultural biogas generation exclusively. ;
UUID: b8bdf4af-0405-365c-b025-9adbc8d8c7ad
Data represents the in- and outputs due to liquid manure and co-substrate pre treatment, digestion and storage of digested manure .  Also the transport of the co-substrate is taken into account.  Gas purification and the use of the gas for co-generation are not included.
Location: Conditions of typical swiss plant.
Technology: Mesophile digestion
Time period: undefined
Production volume: 103787 m3/a
Sampling: Literature data 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_b8bdf4af-0405-365c-b025-9adbc8d8c7ad.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
